WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.640
- Welcome back everybody.

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:04.440
We have Daniel Radcliffe and
Jane Krakowski on the line.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.807
They are both actually in the new

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:08.370
"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt:
Kimmy vs. the Reverend"

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:09.210
now on Netflix.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.550
Go and check it out.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.090
Because the new Kimmy Schmidt episode

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.198
is about making choices,
and because Twitter

00:00:14.198 --> 00:00:16.740
forces tough questions upon us everyday,

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:18.670
Daniel, Jane and I are going to deal

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.620
with some of those very tough choices

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.955
in a little segment called:

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.911
"Kelly's Quaran-Twitter Questionnaire."

00:00:24.911 --> 00:00:27.740
(high intensity techno music)

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.750
I'll read some of the most
liked and retweeted questions

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:30.930
on Twitter in the last month.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.490
Then, we will all get to answer.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:36.287
So, our first Twitter question
is from @theyearofelan.

00:00:36.287 --> 00:00:39.487
"Your quarantine nickname
is how you feel right now

00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:42.510
"plus the last thing you
ate out of the cupboard."

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.050
Okay Jane, you go, ladies first.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:44.883
Go ahead.

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:45.912
- Oh. Okay.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:49.801
Mine would be hopeful Nut Thins.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:53.020
(laughs)

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:53.897
- That's amazing.

00:00:53.897 --> 00:00:54.730
Daniel, what's yours?

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:56.880
- I was going to say,
mine I guess would be like

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.660
contented honey roasted almonds.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.846
It's quite long.

00:00:59.846 --> 00:01:02.090
(laughs)
- Oh, I like that though.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:02.923
- Okay.

00:01:02.923 --> 00:01:05.535
Mine is overwhelmed red velvet cake.

00:01:05.535 --> 00:01:07.618
(laughs)

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.413
But you know what?

00:01:09.413 --> 00:01:11.793
You usually do feel overwhelmed
when you eat too much of it.

00:01:11.793 --> 00:01:13.210
A friend told me.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.343
I obviously haven't eaten too much.

00:01:15.343 --> 00:01:20.343
All right so next Twitter
question is from @GifMario.

00:01:21.027 --> 00:01:25.198
"Who is your racer of choice
in Mario Kart on Nintendo 64?"

00:01:25.198 --> 00:01:26.323
(gasps)

00:01:26.323 --> 00:01:27.830
Daniel, what's yours?

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:28.663
You're the gamer.

00:01:28.663 --> 00:01:30.820
- I was never very good at it,

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.360
but I think the character that I always

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.620
liked playing as the most was Yoshi.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.453
- I love Yoshi!

00:01:35.453 --> 00:01:36.320
- I think I would go for that

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.950
just cause he was like cute and fun.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.240
- Yeah, Yoshi's cool.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.140
That would have been mine.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.030
Yoshi's mine.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:42.863
What's yours, Jane?

00:01:42.863 --> 00:01:43.720
Have you ever played Mario Kart?

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.330
- I've never played it.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.250
I somehow did not get into
the video game thing at all

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.850
and I know with kids, the kid pressure

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.750
my son hasn't really gotten
into them yet either.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.480
I'm sort of trying to slow that down.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.404
But so, I'll take Yoshi too.

00:01:57.404 --> 00:01:58.530
(laughs)

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.363
- Yoshi's awesome.

00:01:59.363 --> 00:02:01.187
Yoshi's, it's a fun one.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:04.453
This next one was posted
by @movingsideways.

00:02:06.097 --> 00:02:08.277
"You are quarantined with the first artist

00:02:08.277 --> 00:02:10.126
"you saw in concert, who is it?"

00:02:10.126 --> 00:02:12.488
Daniel I'll let you go first.

00:02:12.488 --> 00:02:17.220
- Well, the first band I
went to see was the Strokes,

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.910
which is quite cool,

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.760
but the actual real answer,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.740
which is that a concert I was taken to,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.260
when I was like 10,

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.900
would be the Pet Shop Boys.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.449
So it would be me and the Pet Shop Boys.

00:02:28.449 --> 00:02:30.610
- Wow! Those are both pretty cool.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.390
- Yeah, they're both pretty cool.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.969
- Yeah, okay, you're cool, whatever.

00:02:33.969 --> 00:02:36.790
(laughs)
What was yours, Jane?

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:38.350
- Mine's a little more Jersey,

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.413
where I was raised.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.539
My band is Van Halen.

00:02:42.539 --> 00:02:44.500
- Oh, that's amazing!

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.510
- That would be a hell of a quarantine.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.570
- So me and David Lee Roth like,

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:50.080
dancing on the table I guess, I dunno.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.880
- Your quarantine's gonna be a good time.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:53.713
That's amazing.

00:02:53.713 --> 00:02:55.576
- My house is gonna be trashed.

00:02:55.576 --> 00:02:57.826
(laughter)

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.590
- Mine, I honestly can't remember

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:02.423
I know this sounds funny,

00:03:02.423 --> 00:03:03.623
I can't remember,

00:03:07.148 --> 00:03:08.756
this is gonna sound funny,

00:03:08.756 --> 00:03:10.450
but it was either the Toadies,

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.690
which is my favorite band of all time.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:13.456
It's a Texas band, they're alternative.

00:03:13.456 --> 00:03:16.776
Or it's Celine Dion, so
I don't know which one--

00:03:16.776 --> 00:03:17.800
(laughs)

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.330
But I think she'd be a hell of a good time

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:20.504
in a quarantine.
- I think so too.

00:03:20.504 --> 00:03:22.380
- I don't know if you've
seen her on stage,

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.546
but she's crazy funny.

00:03:23.546 --> 00:03:26.040
But, okay, anyway.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.277
Next question is from @cantedcat.

00:03:30.277 --> 00:03:34.780
"Is it bad if I order five
pounds of Mike and Ike's?"

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:35.613
No it's not bad.

00:03:35.613 --> 00:03:36.830
I mean, five pounds of it,

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:39.760
I mean, expect to gain a
good 10 after you eat it,

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.730
but yeah.
(laughter)

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.750
- We're all kinda buying
in bulk right now.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.560
- Yeah, we are.
(laughs)

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.380
What would your candy of choice be

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.550
if you had only one candy
for this quarantine,

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:49.383
just curious?

00:03:49.383 --> 00:03:51.960
- Uh.
- Oh my goodness.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.630
- I know, I actually don't know my answer.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:55.030
- Actually, Daniel will know this

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:55.863
'cause they are my favorite

00:03:55.863 --> 00:03:57.460
and I actually-- this is embarrassing,

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.690
but they're Maynards Wine Gums.

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:03.450
- Oh wow.
- I love Wine Gums.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:05.125
- What does that mean, what is that?

00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:07.555
(laughs)
- It's hard to explain.

00:04:07.555 --> 00:04:09.480
- They're like a--
- A Wine Gum?

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.180
- They're British.
- Yeah.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.960
- We have a great British
store right near me

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.905
that imports stuff from Britain

00:04:14.905 --> 00:04:17.667
'cause I love British
candy for some reason.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:20.830
(mumbles)
- Yeah, so mine would be

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.827
Maynards Wine Gums, but that's so--

00:04:25.146 --> 00:04:27.140
- Wine Gums are incredibly chewy,

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.453
but also somehow very hard.

00:04:29.453 --> 00:04:33.300
They somehow manage to be both chewy

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.436
and hard to chew.

00:04:34.436 --> 00:04:36.286
- You're kinda describing a Milk Dud.

00:04:37.711 --> 00:04:39.170
- Yeah, but they're fruity flavored.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.391
- It's more like a Gummy Bear, but harder.

00:04:41.391 --> 00:04:42.758
- Yeah.
- Ohh.

00:04:42.758 --> 00:04:44.952
- Mine would be
chocolate-covered Gummy Bears,

00:04:44.952 --> 00:04:46.426
now I just thought of mine.

00:04:46.426 --> 00:04:47.585
I love chocolate-covered Gummy Bears.

00:04:47.585 --> 00:04:48.785
- I've never had that, is that good?

00:04:48.785 --> 00:04:49.728
- Does that exist?
- You've never had

00:04:49.728 --> 00:04:50.561
a chocolate-coated Gummy Bear?

00:04:50.561 --> 00:04:52.340
- No.
- No, I've had regular

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.230
Gummy Bears a lot.
- I don't even like

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.150
regular Gummy Bears.

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:56.680
I just like the
chocolate-covered Gummy Bears.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:57.880
I know that's weird.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.460
Anyway, you're amazing and you're welcome

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.980
and I'm sorry.
(laughs)

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:04.830
- What would yours be, Daniel?

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:05.810
- I don't know, any kind of

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:09.600
tiny Mars bar or Snickers.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:10.930
- Like the little bite-sized ones?

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.170
- Yeah, just want some of those

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:13.743
that don't feel like a full chocolate bar

00:05:13.743 --> 00:05:17.043
that you can just hammer
away for hours. That.

00:05:17.043 --> 00:05:18.935
- Yeah, I don't know
what that's like Daniel.

00:05:18.935 --> 00:05:21.018
(laughs)

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.750
All right, well this last question

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.837
is from @jillyhendrix.

00:05:25.837 --> 00:05:27.731
"Has anyone else moved on from wearing

00:05:27.731 --> 00:05:32.731
"sweatpants and is now
just wearing blankets?"

00:05:32.853 --> 00:05:35.103
(laughter)

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.070
What person is walking around their house

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.670
naked right now, that's awesome.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.600
- I got sweatpants on,
I'm sweatpants gang.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.650
- Oh, you're so good.

00:05:46.919 --> 00:05:50.120
I was like, 'I feel weird

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.830
'not having shoes on
while I do an interview,'

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.560
so it's like--
- I love you, Daniel.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.033
- I had to get dressed for this.

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:58.240
- It's still kinda snowy here in Montana,

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.560
and our place is on a ranch,

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:01.070
so I have full-on snow boots

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:04.083
and workout pants on that I'm
totally not gonna workout in.

00:06:04.083 --> 00:06:04.916
- So I have a theory.

00:06:04.916 --> 00:06:06.470
I've had a long-time theory that

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:07.570
you shouldn't wear sweatpants,

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:09.230
or you should wear clothes
that hurt a little bit

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:11.758
just to maintain your weight.
(laughs)

00:06:11.758 --> 00:06:16.050
That's my only weight maintaining advice.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.090
Not diet and exercise,

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.020
just wear something that hurts a little

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.979
so you remember not to overeat.

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:20.812
(laughs)

00:06:20.812 --> 00:06:22.030
And it has gone to the wind.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.560
I don't even wanna know how much weight

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.690
I've gained during quarantine

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:27.750
'cause I'm wearing sweatpants
and leggings everyday

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:29.410
- I know, when you wear elastic everyday

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.420
you just don't know, do ya?

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:33.500
- You just forget.
(laughs)

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:34.570
- Okay, well thank you so much.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:36.780
Everyone, be sure to use
your time at home wisely.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:37.613
And watch

00:06:37.613 --> 00:06:39.470
"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt:
Kimmy vs. the Reverend"

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.270
on Netflix, May 12th.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:42.370
It's gonna be awesome.

